   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Icon Scatter\n\nA field of line icons draws itself over the outgoing scene, covers the swap, then scatters outward to reveal the incoming scene. Built-in placeholder scenes A and B (the two .isc-panel elements) make it preview on its own; to use it between your own scenes, replace the contents of those two panels with your scenes (or set them to your full-frame clips) and keep the block on a track above.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 1.3333 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Playful or app-style pieces where icons are part of the brand.\n- A short cover transition that hides the swap behind a graphic field.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Serious or cinematic content.\n- When the icon set would clash with the brand's own iconography.\n\nVariables:\n- count (number, 4-60): Icon count, default 15\n- color (color): Icon color, default \"#fafafa\"\n- cover_color (color): Cover color, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- cover_opacity (number, 0-1): Cover opacity, default 0.92\n- stroke_width (number, 0.5-4): Stroke width, default 2\n- fly_distance (number, 0-800): Fly distance, default 260\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
